    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The 30k throughput looks promising, but that \"variability in operational continuity\" concerns me. Can you run a more detailed simulation on what happens during a major disruption—like a regional port strike or a massive weather event—under the decentralized model versus the current setup? I need to see if the 50 modules can actually coordinate well enough to prevent life-critical shortages during a crisis.",
